[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3446550186","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112002#issuecomment-3446550186","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112002","id":3446550186,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Nbi6q","user":{"login":"The-Cyber-Captain","id":141319868,"node_id":"U_kgDOCGxevA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/141319868?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain","html_url":"https://github.com/The-Cyber-Captain","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-25T10:44:57Z","updated_at":"2025-10-25T11:30:24Z","body":"(EDIT: Re: Check for class reference updates) What a clever little test. 👏\r\n\r\nWas actually painfully aware I hadn't updated the docs - intending to simply copy the line from joint3d - but wasn't entirely sure how to go about it... having seen some other non documented methods in Production, and this being off my own initiative, I figured that might be for a later date.\r\n\r\nHowever, the error message indicates exactly where I need to update. Again, très clever.\r\n\r\nWill see if I can commit --amend when back at an actual computer later today.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3446550186/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3598708245","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112002#issuecomment-3598708245","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112002","id":3598708245,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Wf-4V","user":{"login":"Marparaman","id":246173075,"node_id":"U_kgDODqxNkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/246173075?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marparaman","html_url":"https://github.com/Marparaman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marparaman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marparaman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marparaman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marparaman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marparaman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marparaman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marparaman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marparaman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marparaman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-01T20:31:12Z","updated_at":"2025-12-01T20:31:12Z","body":"The PhysicsBone3D Joint, which RID i use in PhysicsServer3D.generic_6dof_joint_set_param() is set to 6DOF.\r\nWhen setting parameters through the PhysicsServer3D, I received the following error message: \r\n\r\n@ _physics_process(): Condition \"joint->get_type() != JOINT_TYPE_6DOF\" is true.\r\n  <C++ Source>  modules/jolt_physics/jolt_physics_server_3d.cpp:1532 @ generic_6dof_joint_set_flag()\r\n  <Stack Trace> JOINT_MOTOR_SCRIPT.gd:86 @ _physics_process()\r\n  \r\nI found that printing Physicalbone.get_joint_type() returns 5, while printing PhysicsServer3D.joint_get_type(jointRID) returns 4.\r\n \r\nEverything works as expected, so I avoid the error by asking: if PhysicsServer3D.joint_get_type(jointRID) == 4:\r\n \r\nI then set the parameter.\r\n\r\nIs there a mismatch in how the joint types are being counted?\r\nIf I can offer any help in clarifying this matter, I will be happy to do so. I am a beginner and do not want to cause any unnecessary hassle.\r\n\r\nKind regards","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3598708245/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3626531286","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112002#issuecomment-3626531286","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112002","id":3626531286,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7YKHnW","user":{"login":"The-Cyber-Captain","id":141319868,"node_id":"U_kgDOCGxevA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/141319868?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain","html_url":"https://github.com/The-Cyber-Captain","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-08T11:51:09Z","updated_at":"2025-12-08T11:51:09Z","body":"I know I run a similar check in my specific use case* to only run PI / PID motor control on 6DOF and some other behaviour on NONE... where the joint has been 'broken'. I don't hit any such mapping or off-by-one conditions, though knowing me I likely refer to some defined enums rather than ints themselves.\r\n\r\nHmmm. Let me have a closer look and see if I can reproduce. I suspect, if I can, it's a mismatch outside this PR itself and some legacy issue elsewhere. But I'll investigate today.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n* (admittedly a custom build which adds in another couple of PRs under consideration, with graphs to tune it. #scopeCreep #overkill #exhibitA 🤣 )\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2b0b6533-9a3e-4988-853e-b07d9fa474e2\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3626531286/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3626612920","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112002#issuecomment-3626612920","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112002","id":3626612920,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7YKbi4","user":{"login":"The-Cyber-Captain","id":141319868,"node_id":"U_kgDOCGxevA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/141319868?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain","html_url":"https://github.com/The-Cyber-Captain","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-08T12:11:01Z","updated_at":"2025-12-08T12:11:01Z","body":"Yeah...\r\n\r\nPhysicsServer3D:\r\n\r\n```\r\nenum JointType:\r\n● JOINT_TYPE_PIN = 0\r\nThe Joint3D is a PinJoint3D.\r\n● JOINT_TYPE_HINGE = 1\r\nThe Joint3D is a HingeJoint3D.\r\n● JOINT_TYPE_SLIDER = 2\r\nThe Joint3D is a SliderJoint3D.\r\n● JOINT_TYPE_CONE_TWIST = 3\r\nThe Joint3D is a ConeTwistJoint3D.\r\n● JOINT_TYPE_6DOF = 4\r\nThe Joint3D is a Generic6DOFJoint3D.\r\n● JOINT_TYPE_MAX = 5\r\n```\r\n\r\nand\r\nPhysicalBone3D:\r\n\r\n```\r\nenum JointType:\r\n● JOINT_TYPE_NONE = 0\r\nNo joint is applied to the PhysicsBone3D.\r\n● JOINT_TYPE_PIN = 1\r\nA pin joint is applied to the PhysicsBone3D.\r\n● JOINT_TYPE_CONE = 2\r\nA cone joint is applied to the PhysicsBone3D.\r\n● JOINT_TYPE_HINGE = 3\r\nA hinge joint is applied to the PhysicsBone3D.\r\n● JOINT_TYPE_SLIDER = 4\r\nA slider joint is applied to the PhysicsBone3D.\r\n● JOINT_TYPE_6DOF = 5\r\nA 6 degrees of freedom joint is applied to the PhysicsBone3D.\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis appears to be a mismatch in defining those enums, separate to this particular PR and likely needs to be addressed in a discussion or proposal. 🫤 \r\n\r\n@Marparaman , for your particular case - in the immediate term - I'd recommend relying upon the appropriate enum for each class instead. Eg,\r\n\r\n```\r\n\tif PhysicsServer3D.joint_get_type(jointRID) == PhysicsServer3D.JOINT_TYPE_6DOF:\r\n\t\t# do whatever\r\n```\r\nAnd similarly for any setting / changing of joint type. Hope this helps!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3626612920/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3651766452","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112002#issuecomment-3651766452","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112002","id":3651766452,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ZqYi0","user":{"login":"Marparaman","id":246173075,"node_id":"U_kgDODqxNkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/246173075?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marparaman","html_url":"https://github.com/Marparaman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marparaman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marparaman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marparaman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marparaman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marparaman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marparaman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marparaman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marparaman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marparaman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-14T18:01:58Z","updated_at":"2025-12-14T18:01:58Z","body":"@The-Cyber-Captain Thank you for your response and for implementing this great feature. I used it with different systems to create active ragdolls.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/83e8ad46-8ed0-4b51-8158-10d75a69ca44\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3651766452/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":2,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3651818559","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112002#issuecomment-3651818559","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112002","id":3651818559,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ZqlQ_","user":{"login":"The-Cyber-Captain","id":141319868,"node_id":"U_kgDOCGxevA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/141319868?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain","html_url":"https://github.com/The-Cyber-Captain","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-14T19:02:23Z","updated_at":"2025-12-14T19:02:23Z","body":"> \"I used it with different systems to create active ragdolls.\"\r\n\r\nMe too. 😄\r\n\r\n(Some of the pure 'spring' force approaches were fun; energetic and numerically stable... ish. But looks like joint-motor with PID is likely to be the route I take in the first couple of projects I have in mind. Combined with 4.6's touted IK Skeleton Modifier, Jolt Physics, and - my personal fascination - XR tracking.. there's some very fun character and gameplay experiences to leverage here.)\r\n\r\nI look forward to seeing more of your work @Marparaman, and glad I could help.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3651818559/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4415279370","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112002#issuecomment-4415279370","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112002","id":4415279370,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABByvRCg","user":{"login":"brynm0","id":11431330,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNDMxMzMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11431330?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brynm0","html_url":"https://github.com/brynm0","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brynm0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brynm0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brynm0/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brynm0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brynm0/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brynm0/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brynm0/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brynm0/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brynm0/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-10T12:26:14Z","updated_at":"2026-05-10T12:26:14Z","body":"Seconding a use case for this. When trying to work w/ procedurally animated skeletons, where I have a PhysicalSkeleton3D that animates by driving toward a target pose, I'm currently forced to use a fairly jank setup where I apply a force/torque in the PhysicalBone3D's _integrate_forces callback. It kind of works, but I'm not a physics programmer and it's got tons of stability issues. This would be broadly solved if I could get the joint's RID, which would then allow me to set the motor params in PhysicsServer3D for a more neatly integrated solution (i.e. the motor solver is smarter than anything I can write in _integrate_forces!). ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4415279370/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4768855157","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112002#issuecomment-4768855157","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112002","id":4768855157,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABHD70dQ","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-22T13:34:35Z","updated_at":"2026-06-22T13:34:35Z","body":"Thanks! Congratulations on your first merged contribution! 🎉 ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4768855157/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":2,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]